*VERSION: 3.0
*WRITTEN_BY: openair-conformance
* Tests: AA SR/SS and AA SS/SR at 20 degrees north, 96 degrees east. Sunrise is just after 00:00Z on some days and just before 00:00Z on other days. A window with a sun event belongs to a local solar day (local solar time is UTC + 6:24 here), so the window does not move to another day.

AC D
AY TRA
AN Example TRA 1
AA SR/SS
AH 4500 FT AMSL
AL GND
DP 20:05:00N 095:55:00E
DP 20:05:00N 096:05:00E
DP 19:55:00N 096:05:00E
DP 19:55:00N 095:55:00E
DP 20:05:00N 095:55:00E

AC D
AY TRA
AN Example TRA 2
AA SAT,SUN SS/SR
AH 4500 FT AMSL
AL GND
DP 20:05:00N 095:55:00E
DP 20:05:00N 096:05:00E
DP 19:55:00N 096:05:00E
DP 19:55:00N 095:55:00E
DP 20:05:00N 095:55:00E
